#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# graphics3d

#% text
# `graphics3d(content)` is a three-dimensional graphic of primitives and directives, seen in perspective, lit, in a box.

#% text
# `graphics3d(content, options...)` takes options such as `axes`, `view_point`, `box_ratios`, `plot_range`, `boxed`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The primitives are `sphere`, `ball`, `ellipsoid`, `cuboid`, `cylinder`, `cone`, `tube`, `polygon`, `triangle`, `line`, `point`, `arrow` and `text`; directives (colours, `opacity`, `thickness`, `point_size`, `edge_form`, `face_form`) work as in two dimensions.

#% item
# Faces are lit by a soft ambient light, a key light from the upper left and a fill light, and drawn far to near; the picture is drawn like any graphic, so PNG, SVG and PDF agree and labels are typeset.

#% item
# Like `graphics`, a value is shown as its picture: a PNG with SVG and PDF copies; `export_data` writes it.

#% item
# `view_point: [x, y, z]` is the eye in units of the box (default `[1.3, -2.4, 2]`); `front`, `back`, `left`, `right`, `above`, `below` name views along the axes.

#% item
# Options nothing reads are left out.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A sphere:

#% cell
graphics3d(sphere())
#% output
#= image("graphics3d.files/graphics3d-1.png")

#% text
# Primitives side by side, with axes:

#% cell
graphics3d([sphere(), red, cuboid([2, -0.5, -0.5]), blue, cylinder([[4, 0, -1], [4, 0, 1]], 0.5)], axes: true)
#% output
#= image("graphics3d.files/graphics3d-2.png")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Lines, points, arrows and text:

#% cell
graphics3d([thick, line([[0, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1]]), point_size(large), point([1, 0, 1]), arrow([[0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 1]]), text("$z$", [0, 0, 1.15])])
#% output
#= image("graphics3d.files/graphics3d-3.png")

#% text
# A translucent polygon over a cone:

#% cell
graphics3d([cone([[0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 1]], 0.5), opacity(0.5), orange, polygon([[-1, -1, 0.5], [1, -1, 0.5], [1, 1, 0.5], [-1, 1, 0.5]])])
#% output
#= image("graphics3d.files/graphics3d-4.png")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# Seen from above, without the box:

#% cell
graphics3d([sphere(), cuboid([1, 1, -1])], view_point: above, boxed: false)
#% output
#= image("graphics3d.files/graphics3d-5.png")

#% text
# Axis labels with math:

#% cell
graphics3d(cuboid(), axes: true, axes_label: ["$x$", "$y$", "$z$"])
#% output
#= image("graphics3d.files/graphics3d-6.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sphere`, `cuboid`, `plot3d`, `graphics`
